{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
  "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do you -- am I to take that your -- I think what I read from your brief is that we should draw the line that we drew in Bagli between compensatory damages under the contempt inherent power and punishment damages that require criminal civil procedures. Is that the same thing you're asking us to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes. That's essentially the same thing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Wasn't, that wasn't that what was found here was that it was pervasive from the very first effort to get discovery continuing through the settlement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why was that causal decision by the district court wrong?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, we think that they could recover for that expert. And, in fact, you know, the district court never got into the actual analysis of causation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "back to the question that the Chief Justice asked you. You said that you favored the approach of Fox v. Vice, which is a but-for test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: What costs do you concede you're responsible for?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BERGERON: We would concede we are responsible for the direct harm flowing from the misconduct that the district court found. And that would include the expert discovery, the deposition of Mr. Osborn and any related preparation or follow-up to that deposition, the efforts to get the tests, if there was discovery requests or negotiations or discovery, perhaps a status conference, the Olsen deposition where the district court found misconduct in the preparing for and following up on that deposition, and then the hearings where the misconduct occurred and any preparation for those."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So how much is that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BERGERON: I don't have a number for you, Justice Kagan."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But that's not anything like the full 2 million?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BERGERON: It's not. It would not be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: You said you wanted to use the Fox v. Vice standard, and part of that is the but-for causation inquiry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What do you -- what do you do then with the plaintiff's position that this case would have settled much earlier, which the district judge accepted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BERGERON: And we would say that that's an inappropriate basis for the reasons I said earlier, an inappropriate basis as a substitute for causation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Suppose there was a finding made in another case that the case would have settled much earlier. Then what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you describe for me your definition of direct causation or causation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Egbert (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. EGBERT: Causation, Your Honor. I prefer causation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goodyear",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Goodyear in its -- in its reply brief, details the good-faith defenses it had that were unrelated to the Heat Rise test; in other words, about the cause of the accident, whether other parties were involved, that the tire was already damaged, the -- you know, all sorts of other things, including ones that went to the question of damages, which surely would have been pertinent in whether the case would have settled."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goodrich",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Goodrich's argument that the defect in the tire, all of that was beside the point because the cause of the accident was road debris? Road debris forced this car to swerve off the road."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, that is a pure legal question. And where -- where do you stand on that? I mean, that, it seems, on the basis of the precedent -- Rule 11, the mineworkers, and so forth -- the answer to that question is no, unless you're going to criminal proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9503032b1d1f568301ae725d73fb1591e4d624946f606a87da455d3f742f8ba9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9503032b1d1f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1406",
